      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "From my experience, it happens when the instance I am trying to join fails to connect. My game decides to try again automatically, but fails and results in me spawning into the world out of bounds, unable to move or open the game menu, with the error sound blaring into my ear until I forcibly close VRC.\n\nI have a satellite internet provider (not the kind that needs a signal from space, the kind that gets a signal from an antenna about 20-30 miles away) at my rural home, which can temporarily disconnect if I'm unlucky. I think it has something to do with the connection to VRC servers being lost in poor network conditions while loading an instance.\n\nPerhaps a new failsafe is needed here to not hurt people's ears. I'd happily take the error world over this bug - at least that felt like an easter egg lol",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
